# Bayusuta Default Parameters

# IPC Bridge on USART2 (SERIAL1)
# MAVLink2 at 1.5Mbps to communicate with Bayusuta-Periph
SERIAL1_PROTOCOL 2
SERIAL1_BAUD 1500

# RC Input on USART3 (SERIAL2)
# TODO: [User Tweak] Adjust if RC input uses a different UART or protocol
SERIAL2_PROTOCOL 23
SERIAL2_BAUD 115

# Battery Monitor 1 (Analog)
# PC2_C and PC3_C
BATT_MONITOR 4
BATT_VOLT_PIN 18
BATT_CURR_PIN 19
# TODO: [User Tweak] Adjust these to your physical resistor network scaling
BATT_VOLT_MULT 10.1
BATT_AMP_PERVLT 17.0

# PCA9685 PWM Driver
# Currently attached to I2C2.
# Note: Native PWM out is typically on TIM pins (e.g. TIM4 on PD12-PD15).
# If using PCA9685 for LEDs or via custom Lua:
# NTF_LED_TYPES might need enabling if used for notification.
